WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.750
Hey!

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.710
We’re back!

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.970
Satoshi and Go have returned
from an investigation in the Isshu region.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:32.600
Let me introduce you all
to your newest playmate!

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.890
This is Dredear!

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.600
Be good to her, okay?

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.240
Here.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.700
That just leaves...

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.870
Huh? Kaiross?

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.080
It’s time to eat!

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:50.790
Huh?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.710
Kaiross is acting weird?

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.010
Yeah.
She doesn’t seem happy at all.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.720
She keeps sighing, too.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.350
I wonder if something’s
weighing on her...

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.220
You know what always cheers me up?
A good battle!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.680
Or, wait...
Didn’t she not like battles?

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.650
I know!

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.770
If I get Heracross to encourage her,
she might cheer up!

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:34.210
Ooh, Heracross and Dredear
are already good friends!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.550
That looks more like “madly in love”
than “good friends”...

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.430
Heracross likes
the sweet scent of flowers...

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.020
Which means
he likes Dredear, too...

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.060
Could it be...?

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.940
That’s why Kaiross is upset!

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:54.020
She thinks Dredear stole
her beloved Heracross!

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.400
Wha—?!

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.570
Hey, Go!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.040
Kaiross!

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.620
Hey, wait!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.380
She does look pretty sad...

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.920
What should I do?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.890
I can’t just tell Heracross and Dredear
to not be friends with each other...

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.030
What happened?

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:49.580
She’s probably thinking,
“If only I had flowers like Dredear”...

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.750
Ah...

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.250
Kaiross... You’re a lovely girl,
and you’re really kind.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.550
There has to be something
I can do for her!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.090
Go!

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.760
What I’d do is eat with her,
and then train with her!

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.140
No, I think we need to be
a bit more considerate...

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.850
“Pokémon Flower Arranging Class
looking for students.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:16.020
“Are you interested in discovering the wonders
of flowers alongside your partner Pokémon?”

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.400
That does sound interesting.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:19.360
Right?

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.190
If I go there,
I might even get to meet Leafia.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.490
Can I go?

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:24.660
Yes, go ahead.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.990
Hooray!

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.160
Isn’t that great news, Eevee?

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:28.990
That’s it!

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.080
Go?!

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.330
The wonders of flowers
with Pokémon!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:36.880
If Kaiross learns all about flowers,
that could help her get along with Heracross!

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.540
Ooh!
That could work!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.460
Huh? What’s going on?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.010
Oh, so Kaiross
has a rival in love.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.930
That’s why I want to cheer her on.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.430
And that’s why you’re going
to a flower arranging class!

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.810
Yeah, I don’t see why not.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.730
But it’s being held at Tamamushi Gym.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.060
Isn’t that a Pokémon Gym?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.150
The Gym Leader’s Miss Erika.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.860
She uses Grass types.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.980
Wait, Satoshi, you know her?!

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.780
We went and battled her before,
right, Pikachu?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.700
Wow...

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.200
So this is Tamamushi Gym...

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.910
Something here smells
really nice!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.170
Excuse me! We’re here to participate
in the Pokémon Flower Arranging Class.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.590
Okay. If you could
fill out this form, then.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.260
Pikachu,
do you want in, too?

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.430
Welcome to Tamamushi Gym.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:34.350
I am the Gym Leader here.
My name is Erika.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.850
<i>We’re excited
to learn with you today.</i>

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.650
Likewise.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.360
Hmm?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.400
If I’m not mistaken,
are you not...?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:43.360
I’m Satoshi!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.490
Right, Mister Satoshi!

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:51.240
You helped rescue the Pokémon
that time the Gym caught fire.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.040
I’m ever so grateful
for your help that day.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.120
It was nothing...

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.250
Huh? Is that true?

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:03.630
So, am I to understand you are all here today
for the Pokémon Flower Arranging Class?

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:07.630
And your partners are
Pikachu, Eevee, and Sarunori.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.220
Oh, no.
My partner today will be...

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.680
My, a Kaiross!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:16.810
Oh, dear.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.900
Um... Is the aroma in the air
coming from the flowers?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.530
It smells great!

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:30.990
Here at Tamamushi Gym, we research the aromas that
Pokémon and flowers emit and make perfumes from them.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:36.620
We extracted that scent
from the leaves of this Leafia.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.500
Leafia. Verdant Pokémon.
Grass type.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.630
Just like a plant,
it uses photosynthesis to produce clean air.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.970
There’s a popular perfume
made from its leaves.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.180
My, my,
what’s this now?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.810
She’s not sure what she wants to evolve into,
so we’re trying to learn as much as we can.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.980
Oh, is that so?

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.860
In which case, you must ensure
you set a good example, Leafia.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.620
Pokémon Flower Arranging
is a new form of art,

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:26.170
in which you decorate Pokémon with flowers
to portray becoming one with those very flowers.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:30.800
First, choose a flower you like
and trim it as needed.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.890
Then decorate
your partner Pokémon with it.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.100
How would you like to decorate
your precious partner?

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.560
What sort of arrangement
would your partner like?

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.560
Make sure that you
fully understand one another.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:49.490
That way, the arrangements you make together
don’t merely show off your love of nature and art,

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:53.070
but also deepen the bonds
between you and your partner.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.820
Wow!

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:54.820
It’s so pretty!

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.700
What do you think, Kaiross?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.410
You can make yourself pretty
with flowers like those, too.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.870
I bet you want to try, right?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.540
It’ll be great, Kaiross!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.290
Yeah!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.800
Once Heracross sees how beautiful
you’ve become, even he will...

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:10.880
Yeah!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.800
He’ll love you so much
you’ll become a couple!

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.800
“Become a couple”?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.020
Are you trying to use Pokémon Flower Arranging
to make someone fall in love?

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:23.310
Oh... No, uh...

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.440
Were my motives impure?!

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:29.900
What a wonderful idea!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.900
Nurturing love between Pokémon...

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:35.950
Please, let me help
however I can!

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.950
Wh-What a relief...

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:45.120
Okay then, everyone, pick whatever flowers you like
and decorate your partners however you wish!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.380
<i>Okay!</i>

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.590
When we came upon
a Flower Arranging class,

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.550
hoping to catch ourselves
plenty of Pokémon...

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:56.550
Finding the brat boys
are at the same place...

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.220
What a surprise, meow.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.470
Today will be the day
we catch Pikachu!

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.270
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.210
What flowers would you like, Eevee?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.880
Are you saying
you want the same flowers as Leafia?

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:35.880
I get it.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.380
Let’s give it a try!

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.850
How about this, Pikachu?

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.480
Oh, those are nice, too!

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:47.940
This is getting fun!

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.520
Let’s add loads more, Pikachu!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.150
This looks like something
Heracross might like!

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:56.610
Yeah!
It looks pretty good on you!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.120
Oh, you like it?

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.990
Okay, let’s work with that
as the main flower!

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.660
You can help me too,
Sarunori...

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.540
Huh?

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.660
Hey!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.250
Don’t just go playing around!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.290
Honestly...

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:14.800
What?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.550
i think that’s going
a bit too far...

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.550
Ex-moose me, dearie.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.730
Let us in on this Pokémon
Flower Arranging too, dearie.

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:29.190
What she said!
We’d appreciate it!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.940
P-Purr, meow!

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.480
Come on over.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.030
Your partners are Sonansu and Nyarth,
is that right?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.200
Sonansu and Nyarth?

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.570
Ack!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.080
Purr, meow...

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.620
It couldn’t be.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:54.130
When they let their guard down,
we snatch Pikachu, dearie.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.090
Your wish is my command!

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:01.390
It’s not bad,
but it’s still missing something...

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.510
Let’s see...

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.970
Buds, huh?

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.980
But if they’re not blooming...

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:12.480
So, if I put this flower here...

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:15.150
And then, on your back...

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:17.900
Oh, this is hard...

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:24.240
I’m sorry, Eevee!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.200
Huh?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.910
It didn’t come out
too pretty...

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.210
What went wrong?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.090
The moment we get a chance,
we grab it, dearie.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.800
Yeah, I know.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.550
Look at this, Nyarth.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:44.890
Sorry!

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:46.260
Don’t worry about it, meow.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.350
Huh?

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.020
Don’t worry about it, meow-I said!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.020
Don’t worry about it, meow-dearie!

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:51.060
Right...

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.650
Pokémon each have their own
nature and characteristics.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:59.030
Lively Pokémon go well with
bright and bold displays.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.400
Meeker Pokémon are better served by
graceful and calm displays.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:06.780
Why not try coming up with performances
that make the most of their characteristics?

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:09.080
Make the most
of their characteristics, huh...

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.290
Can I use these, too?

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.540
Coming up with performances...

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.750
Hmm...

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.800
That’s it! I’ve got it!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:27.430
All of you look like you’ve had
plenty of fun with your partners.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.470
Now then,
let’s take a look at the results!

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:31.810
First up is...

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.020
Huh?

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:34.350
Excuse me,
where are you going?

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.310
Ack!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.650
W-We just thought we’d go
and pick some flowers, dearie!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:43.150
That’s right. We’re picking flowers,
you simpleton!

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.370
I beg your pardon!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:47.410
Dearie, dearie!

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.290
I wonder what
they came here for.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:54.290
With the brat boy
sticking by his side,

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.920
we don’t have any hope of
sneaking out Pikachu...

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.630
This is such a pain.
Let’s just grab him by force!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:00.710
Right.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.920
Vending, come on!

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.310
Rocket...

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:12.850
Vending...

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.730
Secret!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.190
What’re we gonna get?!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.360
The Bloom Sickle Pokémon,
Larantes!

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.070
The Nurturing Pokémon,
Hahakomori!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.780
Begin the operation, dearie!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.200
You got that right!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.040
Now then, Koharu, proceed.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.250
Right. Eevee!

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.840
My!

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:46.340
You went for an arrangement matching Leafia’s
that also takes advantage of Eevee’s characteristics.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:49.140
You’ve made Leafia happy, too!

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.430
Oh, that’s great!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:51.640
Wow...

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.100
They look identical!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:55.890
Very well, you’re next, Satoshi.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:56.690
Yeah!

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:57.730
Pikachu!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.400
What?

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.570
Pikachu, use 100,000 Volts!

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.740
Amazing!

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.580
How gorgeous!

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:17.830
A performance only
an Electric-type Pokémon can do!

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:21.420
I thought that’d make the most
of Pikachu’s characteristics!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.750
Pretty good.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.710
But I’ve got the better idea!

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.090
Right, then.
Go, please start.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:27.800
Right!

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:28.970
Kaiross!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.350
That’s so cute!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:38.350
It is!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.440
It’s not done yet!

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.480
For the finishing touch,
go for it, Sarunori!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:58.830
It’s beautiful!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.290
That’s marvelous!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:06.840
You must deeply understand
both Kaiross and Sarunori to create this!

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.470
If only Heracross
could’ve seen this, too...

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:14.300
Actually, I brought
Heracross with me, too!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.180
Really?!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:18.980
They’ll be face to face!

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:19.890
I can’t wait!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:23.270
Even I’m getting excited
to see this.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.900
Come on out, Heracross!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.240
Pikachu!

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.120
What’re you doing?!

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:42.750
If you say “What’re you doing?!“

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.790
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.670
To protect the world from devastation.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:52.680
To preserve world peace.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.890
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.640
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.180
Musashi!

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.350
Kojiro!

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:04.940
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.150
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.490
Just kidding, meow!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.120
Team Rocket!

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.240
Gah, I knew it!

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.700
I <i>thought</i> you were strange!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.910
We’ve grabbed Pikachu, meow.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.500
And we’ll be taking
the rest of the Pokémon, too!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.420
Hahakomori! String Shot!

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.840
I will not let you
do as you please in my Gym!

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:33.550
Leafia! Razor Leaf!

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:40.100
Pikachu!
Break out with Iron Tail!

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.150
Larantes! Leaf Blade!

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.860
Heracross! Fury Attack!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.700
Leafia! Razor Leaf!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:05.540
Yeah!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.630
Eevee! Razor Leaf!

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:12.590
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:21.430
Larantes! Petal Blizzard!

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.980
Solar Beam!

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.320
Here it comes, Heracross!

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.620
Kaiross?!

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.340
Good work, Kaiross!

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.600
Scissor Cross!

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.060
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.650
Awesome!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.530
You did it, Kaiross!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.820
Oh, her flowers...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.910
Kaiross...

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:40.550
Looks like Kaiross’s courage made Heracross
fall in love all over again!

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.390
Yeah.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:43.010
I’m happy for you, Kaiross.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.310
They really do
make a lovely couple.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.770
Everyone, thank you for today.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:55.480
Always remember the love of flowers
and Pokémon in your hearts.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:56.280
Always!

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.860
Thank you!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.450
Oh, and for you, Koharu...

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.620
This is Leafia’s perfume.

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:07.200
I’m hoping you and Eevee
will find a good answer someday.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.960
Thank you!

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:12.080
Through trying their hand
at Flower Arranging,

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:16.340
Satoshi, Go, and Koharu
have deepened their bonds with their Pokémon.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.900
Whoa!
What are you doing?!

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:35.190
U-Uh... Maybe it’s a hug?

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.730
You’re so strong, Kaiross!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:42.360
It appears there may still be more trouble
in store for Kaiross’s love...

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.950
Now, for our next adventure!

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:11.490
Let’s go!

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.500
What should we be doing
as Team Rocket agents?

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:16.250
Part-time jobs day in and day out
to gather operation funds?

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:19.920
Days of writing apologies
and getting yelled at about missions?

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:22.460
Hey, why don’t we just
quit Team Rocket?

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:22.970
Huh?

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:25.050
Team Rocket’s
not all there is to life!

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:25.550
What?!

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:27.220
It’s finally time to choose!

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:28.970
The cogs of a new fate...

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:30.430
...have begun to turn, meow!

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:31.970
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:34.520
Farewell! The Team Rocket Wanderers!
